--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*invalid implicit conversion from 'char \[.*\]' to 'struct basic_string'.*$
^.*is unknown.*$
--
std::string s("ab") -- construction from a string literal.

With the member-typedef conformance fix ([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef],
[class.prop]) basic_string<char> is no longer truncated at its
const_reverse_iterator member typedef, so it keeps its constructors, is not
misclassified as a POD, and the (const char*) constructor is selected; BMC of
the elaborated basic_string now completes with VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
